WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.867
Tesla showed a Roadster

2
00:00:01.867 --> 00:00:03.267
driving upside down,

3
00:00:03.267 --> 00:00:04.667
then briefly airborne.

4
00:00:05.033 --> 00:00:07.100
But those are two different

5
00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:07.933
engineering tricks.

6
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:10.100
Tesla says fans remove air

7
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:11.633
from beneath the car.

8
00:00:11.933 --> 00:00:13.267
Lower pressure underneath

9
00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:15.467
lets outside air press it

10
00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:16.800
against the surface.

11
00:00:17.133 --> 00:00:18.067
Upside down,

12
00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:20.367
that force must beat gravity.

13
00:00:20.733 --> 00:00:22.900
Tesla attributes the airborne

14
00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:25.033
motion to cold-gas thrusters.

15
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:26.700
They release compressed air.

16
00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:28.133
Gas shoots one way;

17
00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:30.267
the car is pushed the other.

18
00:00:30.567 --> 00:00:31.900
Different jet directions

19
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:33.667
can change its motion.

20
00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:35.900
Off-center pushes can turn it.

21
00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:38.567
But the stored gas is limited.

22
00:00:38.867 --> 00:00:40.667
A short, controlled maneuver

23
00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:42.900
is not proof of sustained,

24
00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:43.800
practical flight.
